cd used to change directory
ls used to list files
mkdir used to create folder 
rmdir used to delete folder
touch  used to create file (note every file has extention)
cp used to copy file from one directory to another (eg cp ucc.txt ~/Downloads/)
mv used to move file from one directory to another (eg mv ucc.txt ~/Downloads/) or used to rename file (eg cp ucc.txt file.txt)
nano used for editting (nano 1.txt)
echo used to write txt also (eg echo "love" 1.txt)
cat used to read file  (eg cat 1.txt)
